# Allowlist: the build context is empty unless a line below puts something back.
#
# The Dockerfile copies `requirements.txt` and `*.py`, and nothing else. A
# denylist here has to name every file that must stay out of the image
# (.env, state.json, history.db, a stray notes file), and the one it forgets is
# baked into a layer. With `COPY *.py ./` the wildcard decides what ships, so
# this file decides what the wildcard can see: a new file is excluded until
# someone argues for it.
#
# targets.yaml and .env are bind-mounted at runtime and must never be image
# content; history.db holds every measurement ever taken.
*
!requirements.txt
!*.py
